s memory and terminate it, losing the response and disrupting the connection.\\n- Evidence: `onStdout: (chunk) => void stdout.write(chunk)`; the SDK’s callback consumer continues pulling events without waiting for the writable to drain.\\n- Fix idea: Consume remote events through a pull-based interface and pause consumption until stdout drains. Apply equivalent bounded handling to stderr.\\n\\n### 2. Closing a connection waiting for the start gate does not cancel its turn\\n- Severity: medium\\n- Confidence: high\\n- Location: packages/sandbox-env/src/start-gate.ts:53\\n- What happens: If a connection closes while its `command()` is waiting behind another startup, `release()` has no acquired release function to call. The queued acquisition remains; when its turn arrives, it holds the gate until readiness or the 45-second timeout, delaying live connections behind it. Multiple closed waiters can compound the delay.\\n- Evidence: `release = await gate.acquire()` assigns `release` only after waiting, while `free()` only calls `release?.()`.\\n- Fix idea: Make queued acquisitions cancellable, or record that the gated start was closed and immediately release any subsequently acquired turn without launching.\\n\\n### 3. A stdout failure during the final flush can be reported as success\\n- Severity: medium\\n- Confidence: high\\n- Location: packages/sandbox-env/src/bridge.ts:49\\n- What happens: If the remote process exits successfully but a buffered stdout write fails during the final flush, the flush callback resolves regardless of its error. The bridge can then return the remote exit code, including zero, even though the parent did not receive the complete output.\\n- Evidence: `stream.write(new Uint8Array(0), () => resolve())`; after the exit wins the race, `await flush(stdout)` is not raced against `outputFailed`.\\n- Fix idea: Reject the flush on write errors and treat that rejection as a fatal bridge failure, including errors emitted while the flush is pending.\\n\\n## Areas checked with no findings\\n- Token derivation and bridge environment allowlisting for master-key and cross-sandbox token exposure.\\n- Bridge argument parsing and target selection.\\n- Sequential stdin writes and remote stdin closure.\\n- Sandbox handle cleanup on normal process closure and start failure.\\n\\nEND-OF-REPORT\"}]}\n./docs/research/phase1-apis.md:87:    onLog?: (text: string) => void;\n./plan.md:102:- Fix found by the concurrency test: each bridge is a Node process that needs about 12 s of wall time to cold-start on the orchestrator's 250m CPU limit. With several at once pi-env gave up with \"connection timed out\" (30 s of silence). `sandbox-env` now starts bridges one at a time (`StartGate`). A shared in-process broker would remove the per-session Node start; that is a later optimisation.\n./packages/sandbox-env/test/bridge.test.ts:59:    expect(err().toString()).toBe(\"bridge: ready\\nerr\\n\");\n./packages/sandbox-env/test/start-gate.test.ts:63:    a.onLog(\"unrelated stderr\\n\");\n./packages/sandbox-env/test/start-gate.test.ts:66:    a.onLog(`${BRIDGE_READY}\\n`);\n./packages/sandbox-env/test/start-gate.test.ts:97:    a.onLog(`${BRIDGE_READY}\\n`);\n./packages/sandbox-env/src/index.ts:59:  const connection = new Connection({ command: start.command, onLog: start.onLog });\npackages/sandbox-env/test/reattach.e2e.test.ts:11:import { connectSandboxEnv } from \"../src/index.ts\";\npackages/sandbox-env/test/reattach.e2e.test.ts:20:  const sandbox = connectSandboxEnv({\npackages/sandbox-env/test/conformance.e2e.test.ts:10:import { connectSandboxEnv } from \"../src/index.ts\";\npackages/sandbox-env/test/conformance.e2e.test.ts:15:  const sandbox = connectSandboxEnv({\npackages/sandbox-env/src/index.ts:46:export function connectSandboxEnv(options: SandboxEnvOptions): SandboxEnv {\npackages/orchestrator/test/host-workspace-env.test.ts:12:const sandboxEnv = vi.hoisted(() => ({ connectSandboxEnv: vi.fn(), ensureClaim: vi.fn() }));\npackages/orchestrator/test/host-workspace-env.test.ts:38:  sandboxEnv.connectSandboxEnv.mockImplementation(() => ({\npackages/orchestrator/test/sandboxes-lifecycle.test.ts:13:  connectSandboxEnv: vi.fn(),\npackages/orchestrator/test/sandboxes-lifecycle.test.ts:62:  sandboxEnv.connectSandboxEnv.mockImplementation(() => ({\npackages/orchestrator/test/sandboxes-lifecycle.test.ts:100:    expect(sandboxEnv.connectSandboxEnv).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(2);\npackages/orchestrator/test/sandboxes-lifecycle.test.ts:116:    sandboxEnv.connectSandboxEnv.mockImplementationOnce(() => ({\npackages/orchestrator/test/sandboxes-lifecycle.test.ts:156:    expect(sandboxEnv.connectSandboxEnv).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(2); // the retry closed the old env\npackages/orchestrator/test/sandboxes-lifecycle.test.ts:185:    expect(sandboxEnv.connectSandboxEnv).not.toHaveBeenCalled(); // the call waits for the new Pod\npackages/orchestrator/test/sandboxes-lifecycle.test.ts:189:    expect(sandboxEnv.connectSandboxEnv).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(1);\npackages/orchestrator/src/sandboxes.ts:5:  connectSandboxEnv,\npackages/orchestrator/src/sandboxes.ts:357:    return connectSandboxEnv({\n<harness>\n[info] Full output: /tmp/tmp-NdChki/pi-output-975c4973-4ef3-40d5-993e-db5c99ceee0c.log\n[warn] Output truncated to its end: 4 lines, 26184 bytes dropped\n</harness>","isError":false}]}
ENTRY 12126 {"id":12126,"kind":"pi.assistant","messages":[{"role":"assistant","text":"[thinking]## Findings\n### 1. Closing during gate acquisition can still return a launch command\n- Severity: medium\n- Confidence: high\n- Location: packages/sandbox-env/src/start-gate.ts:40\n- What happens: If the previous turn has resolved but `command()` has not yet received its release function, closing the connection aborts the waiter. The abort releases its gate turn, but `previous` can already have won `Promise.race`, so `command()` still returns the bridge argv after close. A subsequent waiter can also start while that bridge is starting, defeating serialization.\n- Evidence: `await Promise.race([previous, cancelled])` is followed by returning a release function without rechecking the signal; `command()` assigns that function only after `await gate.acquire(mine.signal)`.\n- Fix idea: Recheck cancellation after the race and before returning the acquired turn, releasing it and rejecting if aborted. Remove the abort listener when acquisition completes.\n\nEND-OF-REPORT"}]}
